## Foundation

The first decisions remain business definition, customer experience, and architecture evolution. Orchestration decisions depend on them; they do not replace them.

{% decision_card number="ADR-0001" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0001-why-beacon-exists-and-business-definition/" %}
### Why Beacon exists and the business definition

Operate Beacon & Co. as a solo digital-presence service around Waynesboro. Begin with a free audit and the smallest fitting paid service. Preserve the founder sales call and client content approval.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0002" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0002-define-brand-and-customer-experience/" %}
### Define the brand and customer experience

Use the forest, sage, gold, cream, ink, and rule palette; Playfair and DM Sans hierarchy; one primary CTA; real photography; visible focus; reduced motion; and honest status language.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0003" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0003-record-architecture-evolution-and-source-atlas/" %}
### Record architecture evolution and source atlas

Keep current and target boundaries explicit. Maintain decision narrative, text diagrams, editable Excalidraw sources, previews, and textual alternatives.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0004" status="superseded" href="/docs/decisions/0004-use-a-durable-ai-assisted-operating-model/" %}
### Use a durable AI-assisted operating model

Originally adopted a file-only handoff and deferred a broker during Phase 1.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0005" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0005-use-astro-for-the-unified-site/" %}
### Use Astro for the unified marketing, docs, and workspace site

Keep one Astro static application with marketing at /, documentation at /docs, and simulation at /workspace.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0006" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0006-use-markdoc/" %}
### Use Markdoc as canonical documentation source

Use .mdoc content entries, a strict Astro collection schema, controlled tags, and unsafe HTML disabled.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0007" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0007-use-central-broker/" %}
### Use a central broker boundary

Implement a separate in-repository broker module as an in-memory simulation. Durable service extraction and live invocation remain future decisions.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0008" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0008-stable-roles-dynamic-models/" %}
### Keep roles stable and assign models dynamically

Define role contracts independently of providers. Assign Claude or Codex per work unit using policy, capability, preference, health, capacity, context, and affinity.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0009" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0009-require-independent-second-voice/" %}
### Require an independent second voice

Use the other eligible provider for critique and exclude the authoring session from approval votes.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0010" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0010-use-deterministic-quality-gates/" %}
### Use deterministic quality gates before model judgment

Run real applicable repository commands before review convergence. A failed blocking gate cannot be outvoted.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0011" status="draft" href="/docs/decisions/0011-use-isolated-git-worktrees/" %}
### Use isolated Git worktrees for live implementation workers

Proposed: when live execution is authorized, assign one validated worktree per work unit. No worktree executor exists now.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0012" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0012-require-human-approval/" %}
### Require human approval for high-impact actions

Pause material architecture, spending, legal/privacy, production, merge, deployment, and release until an authorized human records a scoped decision.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0013" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0013-use-docs-as-code/" %}
### Use docs as code for canonical project memory

Store approved business, architecture, decisions, contracts, workflows, and runbooks in Markdoc. Propose all updates through repository review.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0014" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0014-use-provider-adapter-boundary/" %}
### Use a provider adapter boundary

Compile provider-specific prompts from the same work request and context package. Adapters cannot alter criteria, approvals, or business meaning.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0015" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0015-adopt-secure-cicd-control-model/" %}
### Adopt a secure CI/CD control model

Separate untrusted authoring, deterministic pull-request gates, protected main, immutable artifact promotion, environment approval, production verification, and rollback. External settings remain pending until explicitly activated.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0016" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0016-token-auditor-pilot/" %}
### Pilot a narrow, rule-based token-auditor role

Estimate and tighten context, route Claude or Codex by explicit rules and capacity, and log decisions before considering advanced retrieval or learned routing.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0017" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0017-complete-agent-platform-before-business-expansion/" %}
### Complete the agent platform before business expansion

Finish and freeze a measurable, provider-neutral, policy-gated engineering platform before major business-domain or UI expansion becomes the primary focus.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0018" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0018-bind-prepublication-evidence-to-tree-content/" %}
### Bind prepublication evidence to tree content, not commit identity

Compare prepublication evidence by git tree content hash instead of commit SHA, and run `ci:prepublish` as a real pre-merge required CI check, so the gate can be satisfied by a real merge.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0019" status="approved" href="/docs/decisions/0019-begin-phase-1-6-knowledge-research-understanding-decision-os/" %}
### Begin Phase 1.6: Knowledge, Research, Understanding & Decision OS

Authorize starting the bounded PR-0 increment (schemas, events, typed IDs, privacy/authority invariants) now that Phase 1.5 is verified complete-frozen. Does not pre-authorize PR-0.5 through PR-8 against the known-incomplete spec snapshot.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0020" status="accepted" href="/docs/decisions/0020-authorize-pr-0-5-and-pr-0-6-as-bounded-increments/" %}
### Authorize PR-0.5 (Capacity Watcher) and PR-0.6 (Task Classifier) as bounded increments

Authorize PR-0.5 now, bounded to design plus simulated/unit-tested threshold logic only -- no live provider-capacity polling. Authorize PR-0.6 in scope but gate its implementation start on PR-0A and PR-0B being separately authorized and merged first.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0021" status="accepted" href="/docs/decisions/0021-authorize-pr-0a-and-pr-0b-as-bounded-increments/" %}
### Authorize PR-0A (Architectural Invariants) and PR-0B (Event/Replay Semantics) as bounded increments

Authorize PR-0A now, bounded to the seven contract-checkable invariants (INV-001, 002, 003, 006, 007, 008, 010) plus Section 25A's lifecycle state-machine guards and a contract-consistency test. Authorize PR-0B in scope but gate its implementation start on PR-0A being merged first.
{% /decision_card %}

{% decision_card number="ADR-0023" status="under-review" href="/docs/decisions/0023-define-provider-neutral-execution-budget-semantics/" %}
### Define provider-neutral execution budget semantics

Propose one hard request-scoped meaning for model-call and cumulative output-token budgets across direct, harness, and future ProviderAdapters. Decision preparation only; no runtime, routing, provider, or execution authority is granted while under review. ADR-0022 remains reserved by draft PR #76.
{% /decision_card %}

## Status rule

Implemented and established repository choices may be approved. Target architecture not implemented is draft or under review unless the decision governs a simulation or policy boundary that now exists. Evidence alone does not accept an ADR.
